architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:131:Additional component groups omitted from the first inventory include `components/header/ProjectNameDisplay.vue`, `components/menus/ExamplesMenu.vue`, `components/LoginStatusWidget.vue`, and `components/icons/toolbar/` icon components. `ElementRenderer.vue` is a workspace renderer over legacy structural `ElementTypes` and `worldStore` (`frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue:80`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue:81`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue:83`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue:88`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/ElementRenderer.vue:95`), but it is imported only by `Workspace2D.vue` (`frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:37`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:69`). `Workspace2D.vue` itself imports six non-existent command-class paths (`frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:71`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:72`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:73`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:74`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:75`, `frontend/src/components/workspace/Workspace2D.vue:76`) while the current `frontend/src/commands/` directory contains only `Command.ts`, `CommandStack.ts`, `factories/`, and `operations/`. A source-tree grep found no active import of `Workspace2D.vue`, and only `Workspace2D.vue` imports `ElementRenderer.vue`, so both are dead/uncompilable deletion candidates.
architecture-audit/baseline/inventory.md:133:`frontend/src/utils/` additionally contains `arcGeometry.ts`, `assert.ts`, `formatUtils.ts`, and `rectangleGrid.ts` alongside the transform/projection utilities described above. `frontend/src/commands/operations/` contains `world/`, `processTree/`, `viewState/`, `debug/`, `paper/`, and `toolbar/` subdirectories. `debug/` contains `AddExampleSetupOp.ts`; `viewState/` contains view-state operations; `paper/` and `toolbar/` contain only `README.md`, making them vacant placeholder directories rather than implemented operation families. The paper README identifies only future operations (`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:10`), and the toolbar README likewise lists only future operations (`frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:10`).
architecture-audit/baseline/corrections-round-01.md:9:| Reviewer-A C1; Reviewer-B C1 — inventory missing modules | Addressed | `inventory.md` | Added domain-world support files and descriptor registry (`frontend/src/domain/world/Element.ts:29`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Element2D.ts:1`, `frontend/src/domain/world/Realization.ts:37`, `frontend/src/domain/world/descriptors/DescriptorRegistry.ts:15`), services (`frontend/src/services/GeometryService.ts:21`, `frontend/src/services/InputService.ts:17`, `frontend/src/services/ValidationService.ts:16`), types (`frontend/src/types/ResultTypes.ts:2`, `frontend/src/types/ToolArgumentCollector.ts:17`), operation subdirectories including README-only placeholders (`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:7`), and test breadth. |
architecture-audit/baseline/corrections-round-01.md:12:| Reviewer-B C4 — vacant operation subdirectories | Addressed | `inventory.md`, `quality-report.md`, `risk-register.md` | Flagged `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/` and `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/` as README-only placeholder/deletion candidates (`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:7`-`10`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:7`-`10`). |
architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:71:## Dead code, TODOs, and obsolete surfaces
architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:73:### Q15. TODOs document incomplete behavior in user-facing paths
architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:75:`App.vue` has unimplemented highlight/clear-highlight handlers and a TODO for error feedback (`frontend/src/App.vue:641`, `frontend/src/App.vue:650`, `frontend/src/App.vue:680`). `PaperService` has TODOs for visibility/infeasibility and missing element types (`frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:202`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:238`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:343`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:437`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:610`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:888`). `SVGRenderer` has a TODO around actual canvas dimensions (`frontend/src/services/SVGRenderer.ts:220`). These TODOs sit on rendering/feedback paths and should either become explicit wave scope or be deleted if obsolete.
architecture-audit/baseline/quality-report.md:126:`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/` and `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/` contain only `README.md` files and no operation implementations. The paper README's concrete content is a "Future Operations" list (`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:10`), and the toolbar README has the same future-only shape (`frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:10`). Under the current no-backcompat/aggressive-deletion priorities, these are dead specification placeholders unless a wave immediately implements them. They should be deleted rather than preserved as aspirational architecture.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:48:8. **Components not mentioned** — components/header/ProjectNameDisplay.vue, components/menus/ExamplesMenu.vue, components/icons/toolbar/ (28 Vue icons + index.ts), components/LoginStatusWidget.vue.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:49:9. **`commands/operations/` subdirectories** — Only `world/` and `processTree/` operation directories are described. `debug/` (AddExampleSetupOp.ts), `paper/` (README-only, planned operations), `toolbar/` (README-only), `viewState/` (ViewStateOperations.ts) are unmentioned.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:125:4. **Q17 (Debug logging)** — Agreed with reviewer-A that debug logging is weighted at the same level as type-safety and domain coupling, which overweights it. Most are `console.log` statements that are trivial to remove, not architectural concerns.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:127:5. **Additional quality finding**: `commands/operations/paper/` and `commands/operations/toolbar/` contain only README files describing aspirational operations that have never been implemented. These are vacant placeholders that should be flagged for deletion under the project's aggressive deletion priority.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:160:- The e2e test files that reference `Workspace2D` (`basic-construction.spec.ts`, `distance-transport.spec.ts`) only mention it in TODO comments, not in actual test code.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-b.md:165:The `commands/operations/paper/` and `commands/operations/toolbar/` subdirectories contain only README.md files describing aspirational operations never implemented. These are vacant placeholders without any actual operation files. Under the project's aggressive deletion priority, they should be identified as deletion candidates.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-02-reviewer-b.md:20:| C4 — Vacant operation directories | Flag paper/ and toolbar/ as README-only deletion candidates | **Addressed** | inventory.md addendum identifies paper/ and toolbar/ operation directories as "vacant placeholder directories" with README-only content. quality-report.md adds Q21 specifically for vacant operation directories with path:line evidence (paper/README.md:7-10, toolbar/README.md:7-10). risk-register.md adds R13 flagging them as deletion candidates. I independently verified: `ls frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/ frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/` confirms both contain only README.md files. |
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:55:9. **Components not mentioned**: `frontend/src/components/header/ProjectNameDisplay.vue`, `frontend/src/components/menus/ExamplesMenu.vue`, `frontend/src/components/icons/toolbar/` (28 icon components + `index.ts`), `frontend/src/components/LoginStatusWidget.vue`. While individually small, the icon system and `ExamplesMenu` have service/tool integration implications.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:61:12. **`frontend/src/commands/operations/` subdirectories**: The inventory summarizes `IOperation` and mentions `AddFreePoint2DOp` and `InitializationOps`, but does not enumerate the operation subdirectories (`world/`, `processTree/`, `paper/`, `toolbar/`, `viewState/`, `debug/`) or their contents. Only `world/` and `processTree/` are detailed. The `paper/` and `debug/` subdirectories (containing `AddExampleSetupOp.ts`) are unmentioned.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:121:4. **Q17 (Debug logging)**: While valid, some logging entries (e.g., `console.log('[ActionsPanel] World changed, re-fetching ProcessTree')`) are debug statements that should be removed but represent a trivial cleanup, not an architectural concern. The quality report treats them at the same level as type-safety and domain coupling issues, which overweights their significance.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:148:- `components/header/ProjectNameDisplay.vue`, `components/menus/ExamplesMenu.vue`, `components/icons/toolbar/` (28 files), `components/LoginStatusWidget.vue`
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:150:- `commands/operations/paper/`, `commands/operations/debug/`, `commands/operations/toolbar/`, `commands/operations/viewState/`
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-01-reviewer-a.md:160:The quality-report and risk-register correctly identify that `Workspace2D.vue` imports legacy command-subclass files, but they do not state that **(a) those six imported files do not exist in the tree**, and **(b) `Workspace2D.vue` itself is imported nowhere** (not by App.vue, not by any component, not by any test except e2e `basic-construction.spec.ts` and `distance-transport.spec.ts` which contain TODOs about integrating it). The file is dead, uncompilable code.
architecture-audit/baseline/reviews/round-02-reviewer-a.md:67:- ✅ Additional components (ProjectNameDisplay, ExamplesMenu, icons/toolbar, LoginStatusWidget)
architecture-audit/baseline/risk-register.md:187:**Evidence:** `frontend/src/commands/operations/` contains `paper/` and `toolbar/`, but each contains only `README.md` and no operation implementations. The paper placeholder lists `InvalidateCacheOp`, `SetVisibilityOp`, and `UpdateHighlightOp` only under "Future Operations" (`frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/paper/README.md:10`); the toolbar placeholder similarly lists `SetActiveToolOp`, `SetToolFeedbackOp`, and `SetToolOptionsOp` only under "Future Operations" (`frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:7`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:8`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:9`, `frontend/src/commands/operations/toolbar/README.md:10`).
